---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data.mjs";
const options = [
  { name: "Poly Mailers", slug: "poly-mailers", best: "Soft, non-fragile goods", check: "Film thickness, closure and packed size" },
  { name: "Biodegradable Mailers", slug: "biodegradable-mailers", best: "Projects with a documented material requirement", check: "Exact material, test documents and disposal route" },
  { name: "Poly Bubble Mailers", slug: "poly-bubble-mailers", best: "Compact goods needing internal cushioning", check: "Usable inner size and protection test" },
  { name: "Metallic Bubble Mailers", slug: "metallic-bubble-mailers", best: "Cushioned shipping with a distinctive exterior", check: "Finish, print compatibility and inner size" }
];
const schema = { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "Article", headline: "How to Choose a Mailer for Your Product", author: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Welltroy" }, mainEntityOfPage: `${site.origin}/guides/choose-a-mailer/` };
---
<Layout title="How to Choose a Mailer | Welltroy Buying Guide" description="Compare poly mailers and bubble mailers by protection, product type and specification. Learn what to measure before requesting a quote." canonicalPath="/guides/choose-a-mailer/" schemas={[schema]}>
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Buying Guide</div><p class="eyebrow">Buying guide</p><h1>How to Choose a Mailer for Your Product</h1><p class="lead">A mailer should fit the packed item, provide the right level of protection and work with your packing process. These four questions will help you compare the catalogue.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container article-layout"><div class="article-main"><h2>1. What are you shipping?</h2><p>Soft goods such as folded clothing can often use a lightweight poly mailer. Boxed cosmetics, accessories and other compact items may need cushioning. For fragile, heavy or sharp items, test the complete pack; a mailer alone may not be enough.</p><h2>2. What size actually fits?</h2><p>Measure the product after it has been packed, not only the product itself. Allow enough room to insert the item and close the flap without strain. The mailer sizes in this catalogue are outer dimensions, so request usable inner dimensions when the fit is close.</p><div class="guide-callout"><strong>Practical measurement:</strong> Record packed width, length and thickness, then compare them with the relevant catalogue format. For multiple items in one parcel, measure the full group.</div><h2>3. Which finish and construction matter?</h2><p>Consider film, adhesive, color, print area and whether a bubble layer is needed. A metallic exterior affects presentation; its protective performance still depends on the full construction. If environmental terminology is part of your brief, ask for material and test documentation for the exact option supplied.</p><h2>4. What should be in a quote request?</h2><p>Include the product or model, packed dimensions, quantity, destination, artwork and any target material or performance requirement. This gives the supplier enough context to discuss a suitable format and confirm price, minimum quantity and timing.</p></div><aside class="side-card"><h3>Compare mailer types</h3><div class="guide-options">{options.map((item) => <a href={`/products/${item.slug}/`}><strong>{item.name}</strong><span>{item.best}</span></a>)}</div><a class="button" href="/quote/">Ask for a recommendation</a></aside></div></section>
  <section class="section section-soft"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Quick comparison</p><h2>Find a Useful Starting Point</h2></div></div><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Mailer</th><th>Common starting use</th><th>Check before ordering</th></tr></thead><tbody>{options.map((item) => <tr><td><a href={`/products/${item.slug}/`}>{item.name}</a></td><td>{item.best}</td><td>{item.check}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container inner"><div><h2>Have Your Packed Dimensions?</h2><p>Send them with the quantity and destination to compare suitable catalogue models.</p></div><a class="button button-light" href="/quote/">Request a Quote</a></div></section>
</Layout>
